**Finding: COMPLIANT (preferred position) — no redline proposed.**

The Agreement contains a single exclusivity covenant, Section 5.8, and it binds only the counterparty: "Harpoon shall not, and shall cause its Affiliates not to … develop, commercialize or otherwise exploit any Competing Product … in the Territory." That restraint benefits us, so it is not flagged. Section 5.6.1 ("subject to Section 5.8") and Article 7's reference to "in the case of Harpoon, its exclusivity obligations hereunder" confirm the covenant is one-directional.

I checked for any reciprocal or hidden restraint on AbbVie and found none:
- Article 4 gives AbbVie the **sole** right to Commercialize, book sales, appoint distributors and co-promote;
- Section 10.4 (Covenants of AbbVie) contains only an IP-assignment covenant supporting the Section 5.2 licence back;
- Article 12 imposes no post-termination competition restraint;
- Section 2.2 (p0267) limits only AbbVie's JGC final-decision right, not its business;
- confidentiality use limits (Article 9) are ordinary and not a field-of-use covenant.

The Field/Territory wording in the Section 5.1.3 grant is licence scope, not a covenant restricting what AbbVie may build, buy or sell, so it does not engage NONCOMPETE. The preferred element — no non-compete or field-of-use restriction on Customer — is already met.
